    "body": "I agree, this doesn't seem correct. The only thing I can think of is if it's saying something like `<img src=https://example.com/foo/>` is bad and `<img src=https://example.com/foo />` is OK. But point 6 already kind of covers that.\r\n\r\n@zcorpan has a good history of remembering or grokking what this kind of old spec text means, so let's see if he has any ideas. Otherwise, we should remove this.",
