    "updated_at": "2023-03-03T12:11:13Z",
    "body": "> Empty attribute syntax\r\n> If an attribute using the empty attribute syntax is to be followed by another attribute, then there must be [ASCII whitespace](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace) separating the two.\r\n\r\nUnquoted, single-quoted and double-quoted also need a space if followed by another attribute.\r\n\r\n> Unquoted attribute value syntax\r\n> If an attribute using the unquoted attribute syntax is to be followed by another attribute or by the optional U+002F SOLIDUS character (/) allowed in step 6 of the [start tag](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#syntax-start-tag) syntax above, then there must be [ASCII whitespace](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace) separating the two.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<br class=foo />\r\n```\r\n(removing the space makes the slash part of the attribute value)\r\n\r\nThe text in step 6 of start tag is not a \"must\" requirement.",
